  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-value first experiment is to establish a simple, well-understood baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration: no image processing, no aggregation, no fusion, and PCA is a standard, low-risk encoder. This gives a clean reference accuracy for the RNA modality alone. Subsequent experiments can then isolate the marginal contribution of (a) adding image modality, (b) switching to learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), (c) multiprofile + aggregation, and (d) fusion strategy. Starting from the simplest configuration also minimizes confounding variables and failure modes, making it the best uncertainty-reducing choice under a tight 10-experiment budget."
